                  <mrow>
                    <mo>(</mo>
                    <mrow>
                      <mi>x</mi>
                      <mo>+</mo>
                      <mn>3</mn>
                    </mrow>
                    <mo>)</mo>
                  </mrow>
                </mtd>
              </mtr>
              <mtr>
                <mtd>
                  <mtext>opposite signs</mtext>
                  <mspace width="15em"/>
                  <mtext>opposite signs</mtext>
                </mtd>
              </mtr>
            </mtable>
          </mrow>
        </annotation-xml>
      </semantics>
    </math>
  </para>
  <para>Notice that, in the case when \(m\) and \(n\) have opposite signs, the sign of the one with the larger absolute
    value matches the sign of \(b\).</para>
  <br/>
</div>
